---
title: All Allium Frittata
description: All the alliums — leek, shallot, scallion, garlic and onion — with crisp pancetta in a silky, cheese-free frittata. Adapted from Claire Saffitz's All Allium Deep-Dish Quiche (Dessert Person), minus the crust and onion petals.
servings: 6
time required: 45m
source: https://www.ytrecipe.com/recipes/allium-quiche-claire-saffitz-dessert-person
author: Claire Saffitz (adapted)
tags: [frittata, savory, brunch, allium, weeknight]
cuisine: french
course: dinner
---

> Adapted from the All Allium Deep-Dish Quiche in Dessert Person — crust and
> onion petals removed; pancetta swapped for slab bacon. The absence of
> cheese lets the alliums and custard be their full, delicate selves.
> Substitutions: half-and-half = 3:1 whole milk + heavy cream.

In a #10-inch oven-safe skillet{} (nonstick or well-seasoned cast iron), melt
@unsalted butter{2%tbsp} over medium heat. Add @slab bacon{4%oz}(diced) and cook
until crisp and the fat has rendered, about ~{5%minutes}.

Add @leek{1}(white and light-green parts only, sliced), @scallions{4}(white and
light-green parts only, sliced), @shallot{1}(medium, finely chopped),
@garlic{2%cloves}(coarsely minced), and @yellow onion{1}(medium, finely
chopped). Sauté until soft, translucent, and lightly caramelized,
~{10-12%minutes}. Season lightly with @kosher salt{}, stir in @white wine
vinegar{2%tsp} and a generous amount of @black pepper{}, and spread the mixture
into an even layer in the pan.

Meanwhile, whisk together @eggs{8}, @half-and-half{2%cups},
@kosher salt{1.5%tsp}, and @white wine vinegar{2%tsp}. Blend with an
#immersion blender{} until smooth and slightly frothy — this prevents stringy
egg bits and makes the custard silky.

With the pan over medium-low heat, slowly pour the egg mixture over the alliums
and cook undisturbed until the edges begin to set, ~{5%minutes}, gently
drawing the edges toward the center once or twice with a #spatula{}.

Transfer to a 325°F oven and bake until the center is just set (a slight jiggle
is fine), ~{15-20%minutes}. Alternatively, finish under the broiler for
~{3-5%minutes} for a browner top — watch closely.

Cool in the pan for ~{10%minutes} before slicing. Serve warm or at room
temperature. Refrigerate leftovers up to 4 days; reheat gently.
